`the days of the amended annex ו''s stages` MEANS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `the step's day`) `the steps of the 2016 framework, as amended`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `the amended stages after a retirement in` y m IS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y) `is on or after` d) `the days of the amended annex ו''s stages`

-- A row keeps the rule where its X in all, and every cumulative cell, is
-- the amended coefficient at that stage, to a hundredth of a point.
GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ו' row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an amended annex ו' row follows the rule` r IF
        (r's `X in all, as amended`) `is within a hundredth of a point of` (`the coefficient X of 2016 as amended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019) `for a retiree of` y m)
    AND r's `the months it counts` EQUALS (IF (y MINUS 2013) TIMES 12 PLUS m GREATER THAN 60 THEN 60 ELSE (y MINUS 2013) TIMES 12 PLUS m)
    AND count (r's `the cumulative X, as amended`) EQUALS count (`the amended stages after a retirement in` y m)
    AND all (GIVEN p YIELD
                 CONSIDER p
                 WHEN cell FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                     (CONSIDER more
                      WHEN expected FOLLOWED BY none THEN cell `is within a hundredth of a point of` expected
                      OTHERWISE FALSE)
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            (zipWith (GIVEN a, b YIELD LIST a, b) (r's `the cumulative X, as amended`)
                     (map (GIVEN d YIELD `the coefficient X of 2016 as amended on` d `for a retiree of` y m) (`the amended stages after a retirement in` y m)))
    WHERE
        y MEANS r's `the amended row's retirement year`
        m MEANS r's `the amended row's retirement month`

`the amended annex ו' rows that do not follow the rule` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD NOT `an amended annex ו' row follows the rule` r) `the rows of the amended annex ו'`

-- F-framework-2016-amendment-a: every row follows the rule but six — the
-- last months of service June to November 2018. In each, X in all is
-- 45.16% and the two stages after the retirement are 22.58% each, but the
-- cumulative cell of March 2019 prints 22.58%, the December 2018 one's,
-- not their sum. Read: X in all and the stages' parts, which agree
-- (convention reading.consistent): 45.16% from March 2019.
GIVEN r IS AN `amended annex ו' row`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the retirement month of an amended row` r IS
    LIST r's `the amended row's retirement year`, r's `the amended row's retirement month`

`the March 2019 total of a June–November 2018 retiree is printed at the December 2018 one, not X in all` MEANS
        map `the retirement month of an amended row` `the amended annex ו' rows that do not follow the rule`
        EQUALS LIST (LIST 2018, 6), (LIST 2018, 7), (LIST 2018, 8), (LIST 2018, 9), (LIST 2018, 10), (LIST 2018, 11)
    AND all (GIVEN r YIELD     r's `X in all, as amended` EQUALS (45.16%)
                           AND r's `the cumulative X, as amended` EQUALS LIST (22.58%), (22.58%))
            `the amended annex ו' rows that do not follow the rule`

#ASSERT count `the rows of the amended annex ו'` EQUALS 74
#ASSERT `the March 2019 total of a June–November 2018 retiree is printed at the December 2018 one, not X in all`

-- What the encoding reads for those six: X in all, reached in March 2019.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the coefficient X a retiree has under the amended annex ו'` y m d IS
    `the coefficient X of 2016 as amended on` d `for a retiree of` y m

#ASSERT (`the coefficient X a retiree has under the amended annex ו'` 2018 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2019)) `is within a hundredth of a point of` (45.16%)
